# ==============================================================================
# Prevents secrets and unnecessary files from entering the Docker build
# context / image layers. Without this, `COPY apps/api ./apps/api` and
# `COPY apps/web ./apps/web` in the Dockerfiles would bake real .env secrets
# (DB password, JWT secrets, Cloudinary/Razorpay/SMTP credentials) directly
# into the image — .gitignore does not apply to `docker build`.
# ==============================================================================

# Secrets — never let these into a build context
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies (installed fresh inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist

# VCS / editor / OS
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs, coverage, uploads (runtime data, not build inputs)
logs
**/logs
*.log
coverage
apps/api/uploads

# Docs and unrelated tooling not needed at build time
documentation
design
docs
*.md
